## 🛠 Running the Application Locally

You can run the application locally using any of the following modes:

### Mode 1: Microservice Development Mode (Two Independent Processes)

#### 1. Start Spring Boot Backend (Port 8080)
```powershell
cd src/backend
.\mvnw.cmd spring-boot:run
```
*(On Linux/macOS use `./mvnw spring-boot:run`)*  
Backend runs at: `http://localhost:8080`

#### 2. Start React Frontend (Port 3000)
In a second terminal:
```powershell
cd src/frontend
npm install
npm run dev
```
Frontend runs at: `http://localhost:3000`  
Vite automatically proxies all `/api` requests to `http://localhost:8080`.

---

### Mode 2: Single Fat-JAR Mode (Unified Build)

1. **Build Combined JAR**:
   ```cmd
   build.bat
   ```
   *(On Linux/macOS use `./build.sh`)*

2. **Run JAR**:
   ```powershell
   java -jar src/backend/target/*.jar
   ```
   Both React UI and API endpoints are served together at `http://localhost:8080`.

---

### Mode 3: Local Docker Containers (Independent 2-Container Build)

#### 1. Backend Container
```powershell
docker build -t crs-backend:latest ./src/backend
docker run -p 8080:8080 crs-backend:latest
```

#### 2. Frontend Container
```powershell
docker build -t crs-frontend:latest ./src/frontend
docker run -p 3000:3000 crs-frontend:latest
```

---

## ☸️ Global CaaS Deployment

Deploy using the standard CaaS Helm workflow:

```bash
helm upgrade --install crsaitool ./deployment
```

The CaaS pipeline reads `deployment/values.yaml` and deploys two independent Knative services:
- **Backend Service**: `https://<host>/<engagementId>/<release>-backend/`
- **Frontend Service**: `https://<host>/<engagementId>/<release>-frontend/`

